    "rationale": "The 18 h aliquot was re-read at several dilutions. The readings, scaled back by the dilution factor, were 1.247 at 10x (mean of 2 replicates), 1.41 at 3x, 1.292 at 2x and 1.29 undiluted. All are about 1.3 with no upward trend as dilution increases. If the plateau were reader saturation, the diluted samples would read clearly higher than the undiluted one, and they don't. The 3x value is about 9% high, but the 2x value is not, so I treat it as noise. The plateau from 7 h onward therefore reflects true stationary phase, and biomass is at the level the readings indicate."
